  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Undersea Sensor Systems has $245M in contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Undersea Sensor Systems received 18 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $13.6M. Undersea Sensor Systems obligations fell 37.9% year over year. Undersea Sensor Systems historical obligations show variation across recent fiscal years: FY21 was $7.7M, FY22 was $12.1M, FY23 was $2.7M, FY24 was $1.8M, and FY25 was $394M. Undersea Sensor Systems obligations are heavily concentrated in one NAICS market: Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $241M. Undersea Sensor Systems also recorded obligations in Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $2.1M, Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $1.4M, and Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $574K. Current-year totals are partial because FY2026 is fiscal year to date.",
